  "tagline": "PostgreSQL-compatible MPP warehouse that runs on its appliance, any cloud or Kubernetes.",
  "description": "Yellowbrick is an MPP SQL data warehouse with a PostgreSQL-compatible front end and a custom C++ columnar engine that bypasses the OS for flash and memory access. It originally shipped as a high-density appliance and now runs as a Kubernetes-based software stack in AWS, Azure, GCP or on-prem, with storage on object stores and independent compute clusters. It targets enterprises replacing Netezza, Teradata or Greenplum who want predictable performance and deployment choice. In early 2026 its founder left to start a separate lakehouse company, Floe, while Yellowbrick kept shipping releases.",
